Pillar I: Residual Energy Decomposition (R = A - M)\par
Standard activation steering suffers from high semantic noise because raw hidden states (A) mix content with syntax and token-frequency biases. We isolate pure semantic tension R by subtracting the expected independence matrix M:M = \\frac\{F \\cdot C\}\{T\}Where F represents line sum (token intensity) and C represents column sum (channel mass). \par
The residual matrix R = A - M strips away the structural/grammatical baseline, yielding a pure representation of contextual intention.\par
Pillar II: Inter-Channel Z-Score Whitening (Anisotropy Neutralization)Transformer hidden states naturally suffer from representation degeneration (the "cone effect"). By applying an inter-channel normalization against a neutral corpus baseline (\\mu_d, \\sigma_d):E_w = \\frac\{E_\{\\text\{raw\}\} - \\mu_d\}\{\\sigma_d\}\par
The system maps latent energy into an isotropic space, allowing robust cross-domain target matching and translation across distinct semantic neighborhoods.\par
Pillar III: Closed-Loop Entropy Regulation (H(P_t) Homeostasis)\par
Static injection of vector bias (\\alpha v) leads to syntactic collapse when the model needs to output deterministic tokens. Our system regulates steering intensity \\gamma_t dynamically via token-level Shannon entropy:\\gamma_t = \\gamma_\{\\text\{max\}\} \\cdot \\sigma\\left(\\frac\{H(P_t) - H_\{\\text\{target\}\}\}\{\\tau\}\\right)\par
High Entropy (Uncertainty / Drift): \\gamma_t \\to \\gamma_\{\\text\{max\}\}, pushing the model back toward the target coseme.Low Entropy (Deterministic Syntactic Paths): \\gamma_t \\to 0, releasing control to allow natural token completion (e.g., punctuation, code syntax).\par
3. Production Mitigations for Scale (Gemini 1.5 Compatibility)\par
To ensure this framework functions safely in extreme-scale production environments (1M+ context windows and MoE routing):\par
Mitigation A:  Sliding Window Constraint for Infinite ContextCalculating the total mass T across a 2M token context matrix would cause catastrophic HBM memory fragmentation during continuous batching.\par
Solution: We truncate the evaluation of A to a sliding window of the last k tokens (e.g., k=1024).\par
 A_\{\\text\{local\}\} \\in \\mathbb\{R\}^\{k \\times D\}.\par
 Long-range context remains perfectly preserved in the static KV-cache, but semantic steering is calculated in O(1) memory space based on immediate neighborhood tension.\par
Mitigation B: Unified Manifold Injection for Mixture of Experts (MoE)In an MoE architecture, hidden states mid-network are fragmented across different expert combinations, making a unified (\\mu_d, \\sigma_d) baseline impossible to calculate reliably per-token.\par
Solution: The R = A - M sensor and the subsequent \\gamma modulation are applied exclusively at the final dense projection layer (pre-lm_head). At this bottleneck, all expert routing has concluded, and outputs have been summed back into a continuous, unified latent manifold, allowing stable geometric translation.\par
4. High-Value Application Cases\par
Zero-Prompt System Directives (TTFT Savings): Instead of feeding 1,500 tokens of system prompts to enforce tone, formatting,  or domain expertise, a pre-computed target tensor \\Delta E is projected onto W_\{\\text\{head\}\}^T  at request initialization. This drastically reduces Time-To-First-Token and KV-cache overhead.\par
Long-Context Thematic Anchoring: Over 1-million token outputs, models naturally drift from their initial persona or analytical framework. The entropy loop acts as a thermodynamic anchor, gently nudging the model back to the desired semantic neighborhood whenever uncertainty spikes, without breaking factual retrieval.\par
Dynamic Tone Morphing: Allows real-time translation of the output's neighborhood (e.g., smoothly transitioning from an academic tone to a pedagogical tone mid-generation) simply by shifting the target vector \\Delta E, without regenerating the context.\par
5. TPU/JAX Implementation Vectorization (Kernel Fusion)To make this viable in Pathways / XLA:Pre-compilation: W_\{\\text\{head\}\}^T \\cdot \\Delta E is computed once during target registration, reducing token-level operation to a single jax.lax.addcmul.\par
Zero CPU Synchronization: The entropy calculation and sigmoidal scaling execute entirely inside the XLA HLO graph.\par
No Dynamic Branching: Activation utilizes pure probabilistic operations (e.g., jnp.where) to maintain a static execution graph during continuous batching.Appendix A: Mathematical Foundation of R = A - M DecompositionLet A \\in \\mathbb\{R\}_\{+\}^\{k \\times D\} be the non-negative activation matrix captured over the local window k. \par
A is a superposition: A = M + R + \\epsilon.\par
Where M \\in \\mathbb\{R\}^\{k \\times D\} is the structural baseline, R is pure semantic tension, and \\epsilon  is noise.\par
We define total energy mass: T = \\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A \\mathbf\{1\}_D.\par
Marginal vectors for token intensity (F \\in \\mathbb\{R\}^\{k \\times 1\}) and channel mass (C \\in \\mathbb\{R\}^\{1 \\times D\}): F = A \\mathbf\{1\}_D \\quad ; \\quad C = \\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A\par
Under independence scaling, expected structural mass is a rank-1 outer product: M = \\frac\{F \\cdot C\}\{T\} = \\frac\{(A \\mathbf\{1\}_D)(\\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A)\}\{\\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A \\mathbf\{1\}_D\}\par
Proof of Grammatical Bias Cancellation: Subtracting M from A yields R. \par
Evaluating the row marginal sums of R: R \\mathbf\{1\}_D = A \\mathbf\{1\}_D - \\frac\{(A \\mathbf\{1\}_D)(\\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A \\mathbf\{1\}_D)\}\{\\mathbf\{1\}_k^T A \\mathbf\{1\}_D\} = F - \\frac\{F \\cdot T\}\{T\} = \\mathbf\{0\}_k\par
Since R \\mathbf\{1\}_D = \\mathbf\{0\}_k and \\mathbf\{1\}_k^T R = \\mathbf\{0\}_D^T, the residual matrix R is strictly centered around zero marginal sum. High-frequency syntax tokens that generate large norms in A are projected into the nullspace of M, leaving R as a pure representation of inter-channel semantic coupling.Appendix B: High-Performance JAX/Flax Implementation (Sliding Window & MoE Safe)Pythonimport jax\par
import jax.numpy as jnp\par
from flax import linen as nn\par
\par
@jax.jit\par
def extract_local_residual_energy(hidden_states: jnp.ndarray, window_size: int = 1024) -> jnp.ndarray:\par
    """\par
    Calculates R = A - M applying a sliding window for O(1) memory scaling.\par
    hidden_states: [batch=1, seq_len, hidden_dim D]\par
    Returns: [1, D] - mean energy of the residual tension.\par
    """\par
    # Sliding Window: Extract only the most recent 'window_size' tokens\par
    seq_len = hidden_states.shape[1]\par
    start_idx = jnp.maximum(0, seq_len - window_size)\par
    A = jax.lax.dynamic_slice_in_dim(jnp.squeeze(hidden_states, axis=0), start_idx, window_size, axis=0)\par
    \par
    A_pos = A.astype(jnp.float32) - jnp.min(A) + 1e-8\par
    \par
    # Marginals F [k, 1] and C [1, D]\par
    F_vec = jnp.sum(A_pos, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\par
    C_vec = jnp.sum(A_pos, axis=-2, keepdims=True)\par
    T_sum = jnp.sum(A_pos)\par
    \par
    # Independence Matrix M = (F * C) / T\par
    M = jnp.matmul(F_vec, C_vec) / T_sum\par
    R = A_pos - M\par
    \par
    return jnp.expand_dims(jnp.mean(R ** 2, axis=0), axis=0)\par
\par
\par
@jax.jit\par
def compiled_tpu_steering_kernel(\par
    logits: jnp.ndarray,\par
    vocab_bias: jnp.ndarray,\par
    gamma_max: float = 7.0,\par
    h_target: float = 3.8,\par
    tau: float = 0.5\par
) -> jnp.ndarray:\par
    """\par
    Fused logit modulation kernel. Entropy loop applied functionally.\par
    """\par
    last_logits = logits[:, -1, :]\par
    \par
    probs = jax.nn.softmax(last_logits, axis=-1)\par
    log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(last_logits, axis=-1)\par
    H_t = -jnp.sum(probs * log_probs, axis=-1) / 0.69314718 # Base 2 Shannon Entropy\par
    \par
    # Thermodynamic Homeostasis: Sigmoidal scaling\par
    h_diff = (H_t - h_target) / tau\par
    gamma_t = gamma_max * jax.nn.sigmoid(h_diff) \par
    gamma_t = jnp.expand_dims(gamma_t, axis=-1)\par
    \par
    steered_last_logits = last_logits + (gamma_t * vocab_bias)\par
    return logits.at[:, -1, :].set(steered_last_logits)\par
\par
\par
class FinalLayerSteererModule(nn.Module):\par
    """\par
    MoE-Safe Hook Module: Placed at the final unified manifold projection.\par
    """\par
    gamma_max: float = 7.0\par
    h_target: float = 3.8\par
    tau: float = 0.5\par
    window_size: int = 1024\par
\par
    @nn.compact\par
    def __call__(self, final_unified_hidden: jnp.ndarray, logits: jnp.ndarray, vocab_bias: jnp.ndarray, is_active: bool = True):\par
        # 1. Neighborhood translation analysis on recent context window\par
        r_energy = extract_local_residual_energy(final_unified_hidden, self.window_size)\par
        \par
        # 2. XLA-safe conditional routing\par
        steered_logits = compiled_tpu_steering_kernel(\par
            logits, vocab_bias, self.gamma_max, self.h_target, self.tau\par
        )\par
        \par
        out_logits = jnp.where(is_active, steered_logits, logits)\par
        return r_energy, out_logits\lang10\par
}
